    "notes": "A date goes wrong in public: the convertible blows a tyre (our BANG), the tyre sags, she rolls her eyes, a mint rises out of the roll under our NEW! burst and BREEZE label, he chews, grins and winks, the blanket goes over the hood and her head settles on his shoulder, all under the jingle, which ducks under the bang and the announcer over the sunset wide. The music drops out on the cut to the tow truck; crickets through the trucker's deadpan stare, the sit-down, the open palm and the Breeze put in it; the sung \"Feel the Breeze!\" comes in as his head lands on the hero's shoulder and carries into Take 3's packshot with our BREEZE logo and Turn your day around!. Ported from br4/edit.mjs. Nobody speaks on camera: the only voice is the announcer (br-vo.wav); every other line is sung in the jingle. The sung lyrics are lines heard in the jingle and sting clips, in the music's own clock, so moving the music moves them; their words are approximate. The announcer duck runs to 2.9 s after the line, past the end of the music, as the script's volume expression did."
